WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.069
-The vast majority of Senate
Republicans are sticking with

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:05.872
former President Donald Trump
at his second impeachment trial

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.974
despite powerful evidence
presented by the House

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.643
impeachment managers and the
fact that Trump's lawyers

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.911
are very bad.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.046
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:18.017 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.886
So you know how Trump is
currently facing

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.088
an impeachment trial for trying
to steal the election?

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.422
Well now,
it turns out,

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.458
he's also
under criminal investigation

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.293
for trying to
steal the election.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.494
-Breaking news,
the<i> New York Times</i>

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.163
is just reporting that
prosecutors

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.931
in Fulton County, Georgia
have launched

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:35.334
a criminal investigation
into former President Trump's

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.304
January phone call with the
Georgia Secretary of State,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.340
remember, the one where he told
Secretary Raffensperger

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.776
to "find the votes,"
and also, Jim,

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.712
threatened him.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:49.448
To find just enough votes,
notably, to overturn the results

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.217
in that state's election.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.353
-Wow, first he lost Georgia
now Georgia's investigating him.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.823
It's like getting dumped then
finding out your ex

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.192
blocked your number, filed a
restraining order against you,

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.227
and immediately went to Paris
with your brother.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.195
Trump was already under,
last I checked,

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:06.165
30 different investigations,
and he has no plan

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.567
to get out of any of them.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.169
I mean, even El Chapo
had that tunnel built

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.972
under his jail cell toilet so he
could ride a motorbike

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.008
on a built-in track
all the way to a safe house

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.811
where the tunnel went upwards,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.579
so he could crawl out of
another toilet.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.682
if that were Trump,
he'd just be found half stuck

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.184
in a jail cell toilet
trying to download Parler.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.886
And, by the way,
people close to Trump

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.621
have been worried about this
happening.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.289
Not just because he could end up
in jail,

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.593
but because his lawyers, to
quote the great Clarence Darrow,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.194
"suck major butt."

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.963
-People close to the President
have been increasingly worried

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:40.066
that he may face
criminal charges

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.368
as a result of his actions.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.370
The concern here is that
Donald Trump

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.573
has largely exhausted
his legal options

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:49.809
when it comes to
representation.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.211
No reputable attorney,
at this point,

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:55.080
was willing to stick their neck
out for President Trump

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.649
in this impeachment case.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.151
Allies to the President,
one of them telling CNN

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:02.054
that's "he's effed"
if he faces criminal charges.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.624
-It's true that Trump is effed,
because he's always had

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.825
very bad lawyers.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.626
Such is the price of being an
impossible client

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.062
who ignores the advice of
counsel

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.296
and also
doesn't pay his bills.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.432
No one wants to defend you.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.933
Trump probably got his last duo
during a two-for-one sale

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:16.335
at Lawyer's Warehouse.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.971
You're gonna love
the way I leak.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:21.640
And it's not like representing
Trump leads to

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.142
bigger and better things.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.811
You know, Rudy carried his water
and not only did he get stiffed,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:29.715
he also got hit with a
$1.3 billion defamation lawsuit.

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:33.085
And I tip my cap to Dominion,
because it's very funny to

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:36.222
sue someone like Rudy for over
a billion dollars

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.890
when you know
he doesn't have it.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.661
I feel like Rudy buys his pants
with the pockets pre-turned

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.697
inside out,
like a 1930's vagabond.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.265
Also, do you guys have
any of those wallets

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.401
that moths fly out of?

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.269
But when it comes to
embarrassing Trump lawyers,

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.238
it turns out Rudy
is in good company.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.873
Trump's original impeachment
defense team quit en masse,

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.842
when he demanded
that they repeat

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.878
his election fraud lies
during the trial.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.314
So, he had to settle
for two guys named

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:04.150
Bruce Castor and David Schoen,
who I'm assuming

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.218
he saw in a local
Palm Beach commercial

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.687
while he was watching a relay
of the 1996 Masters

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:09.888
on the Golf Channel.

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.991
"Have you inhaled asbestos?
So have we!

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.226
What was this commercial
about again?"

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:16.863
And this is a fun fact,
Bruce Castor is a cousin

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:20.266
of the GOP counsel from the last
impeachment, Steve Castor,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.534
do you remember him?

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.469
The bumbling dufus.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:26.338
The bumbling duff-ess,
who showed up to hearings

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.774
with all of his files in a
grocery store tote bag,

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.744
like he was dropping off a
delivery order from whole foods?

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.447
Just make sure you freeze the
sprouted whole-grain bread.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.749
As a client,
you know you're in a bad spot

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.885
when your lawyers don't even
have briefcases.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.554
It's like, showing up to a
potluck with a handful

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.822
of loose crab cakes.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.557
Sorry,
I couldn't find the Tupperware,

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.460
also it was pretty hot in the
car, so we should eat these now!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.561
But we shouldn't judge
Bruce Castor just

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:52.265
because his cousin Door Dashed
an impeachment trial.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.766
I'm sure he's much more
professional

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.936
and detail oriented,
as evidenced by the very first

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.504
words out of his mouth,

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.106
as the ex-President's
defense lawyer.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:03.476
-My name is Bruce Castor.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:08.647
I am the lead prosecutor --
or lead counsel for

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:10.450
the 45th President
of the United States.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.685
-I'm the prosecutor,
I mean witness,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.587
I mean accomplice,
I mean defendant,

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.190
no, wait, what's it called?
Juror. Am I the judge?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.525
Case dismissed.
Wow, that was easy.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.761
I wish that he had called his
cousin like the guitarist

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.330
at the enchantment under the sea
dance in "Back to the Future."

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.832
"Hey, Steve, Steve, it's your
cousin Bruce Castor.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.068
Remember that new stupidity you
were looking for?

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.704
Well, listen to this --"

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.306
Don't worry though,
he explains the slip up.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.209
-I was an assistant DA
for such a long time,

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.576
I keep saying "prosecutor,"

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.711
but I do understand the
difference Mr. Raskin.

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:42.314
-It's not good when the first
thing you say in court

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:44.850
is that you know the difference
between the defense

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.218
and the prosecution.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.520
It's like your pilot getting
on the P.A. and saying

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.356
"Welcome aboard
the crosstown bus,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.057
wait, no, this is an airplane.

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.893
Don't worry I know the
difference.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:57.630
I was a bus driver, amigo,
so I know what I used to do

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.331
is different from what I do now.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:02.068
Man, driving a bus was easier.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:04.470
Alright. Let's try to
fly like a bird now.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.306
Make sure your seat backs are
upright and tray tables locked

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.843
next stop, 42nd street."

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.144
And then at another point,

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:13.979
Castor tried to reference
something he saw on the news

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.714
and honestly,
I have no idea

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.116
what he was trying to get at.

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:21.788
-I saw a headline representative
so-and-so seeks to walk back

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.857
comments about --
I forget what it was,

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.558
something that bothered her.

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:30.362
-Well, thanks for the specifics,
that was, was very powerful.

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:32.131
I thought this guy was
a slip-and-fall lawyer,

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.433
but maybe he just slipped
and fell on his head.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:37.236
"My compliments to whoever waxes
these Capitol floors,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.771
it's like an ice rink in here."

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.239
This is a historic moment.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.241
It's the first time in history
a President has been impeached

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.443
a second time.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.611
He incited and cheered on
a violent mob

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.080
that breached the Capitol for
the first time in 200 years

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.950
and injured 140 police officers

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.918
in an attempt to overthrow
democracy.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.387
You'd think his lawyers would be
a little more prepared.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.789
Instead,
Castor meandered aimlessly,

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:00.059
like he was auditioning to be on
one of those sleep apps.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:04.997
-United States Senators are
patriots first.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.966
Patriots first.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.034
They love their country.

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:15.641
They love their families.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:21.680
There isn't a member in this
room who has not used the term

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.652
"I represent the great state
of --" fill in the blank.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.655
Why? Because they're all great?
Yeah.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.891
But you think your's is greater
than others

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.927
because these are your people.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:38.497
-I left a voicemail on ecstasy
in 1997 that made

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.866
more sense than this,
what are you talking about?

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.268
The House managers just laid out
a devastating case

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.337
against the President
with harrowing video footage

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:47.272
and you sound like you're
vamping at the end

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:48.874
of a social studies class.

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:51.243
So in conclusion,
Rutherford B. Hayes

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:54.479
was a President, of the
United States specifically.

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.749
And many people don't know this,
but B was actually

00:06:57.749 --> 00:07:01.821
not his middle initial,
it's more like a verb.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:05.057
Like, Rutherford "Be" Hayes.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.694
Hayes of course being slang at
the time meaning President.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:13.299
And it looks like class
be over.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.800
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.870
In fact, the House managers'
opening argument was so good

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.372
that Castor was so unprepared
that at one point

00:07:20.372 --> 00:07:23.642
he turned it over to his partner
and admitted they had to change

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:26.679
course because they didn't
expect the Democrat's case

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.147
to be so strong.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:33.186
-I think that I want to give my
colleague, Mr. Schoen,

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:41.861
an opportunity to explain to all
of us the, the legal analysis

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:45.497
on jurisdiction.

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:47.799
I'll be quite frank with you,

00:07:47.799 --> 00:07:50.102
we changed
what we were going to do

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.972
on account that we thought
that the House managers'

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:55.875
presentation was well done.

00:07:55.875 --> 00:08:01.214
-Uh, in my defense, I've only
ever seen bad lawyers before.

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.415
I only hang out with my cuz.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:06.552
Take me out, Schoen, I'm dizzy.
I need electrolytes.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:09.121
Tell them about People V.
whatever -- Perry Mason crap

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.890
you're always going on about.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.124
Seriously,
what was he expecting?

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:14.226
Did he think this case
was about something else?

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:17.262
"When I saw that video I was
like, whoa,

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:20.900
that's what this case is about?
That is real bad."

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.435
And then Castor turned it over
to his colleague David Schoen

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.938
who, instead of bumming his way
through nonsense like Castor,

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:28.140
decided to go the heinous
ass[Bleep] route.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.509
-This trial will tear this
country apart,

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:34.113
perhaps like we've only seen
once before in our history.

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.348
-I'm sorry are you threatening a
second civil war?

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:39.051
You know that's basically what
Trump got impeached for, right?

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.652
This is like
if O.J.'s lawyers had said,

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:44.757
"You better acquit him or I will
stab every one of you."

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.392
I mean, seriously,
that is despicable.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.794
Impeachment is in the
Constitution!

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:51.797
These guys all act like it's
some left wing conspiracy.

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:54.366
I mean, Ben Franklin signed onto
it and I'm pretty sure he wasn't

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:56.102
some radical Antifa socialist.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:59.104
Dude tied a key to a kite to
find electricity,

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:01.473
which we were all taught
as like a fun story,

00:09:01.473 --> 00:09:03.242
but really it sounds like
something you make up

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.778
to get out of the house during a
fight with your wife.

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:07.980
"We just had dinner with your
parents last week, Deborah."

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.015
"Well, they want to stay over
this time, too."

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:12.684
"You know what? I'm going
outside." "Why?"

00:09:12.684 --> 00:09:16.455
"I need to tie a key to a kite
to catch lightning, okay?

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:17.623
Get off my ass!"

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:19.224
That was a brief excerpt
from my rejected

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:21.093
Broadway musical "Franklin,"
which was supposed to

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:23.195
be the new "Hamilton,"
but you know, COVID.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:24.964
Also, they said
the rapping was bad.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.965
[ Rapping ] ♪ My name is Ben and
I'm here to say ♪

00:09:26.965 --> 00:09:29.101
♪ You need a penny saved ♪

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.236
Schoen went on to claim
that the only reason the trial

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:33.472
was even happening was because
Democrats were desperate

00:09:33.472 --> 00:09:34.740
to impeach Trump.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.242
-In this unprecedented snap
impeachment process,

00:09:37.242 --> 00:09:40.046
the House of Representative
denied every attribute

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:42.614
of fundamental Constitutional
due process

00:09:42.614 --> 00:09:44.716
that Americans correctly have
come to believe

00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:46.852
is part of what makes this
country so great.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:48.687
How and why did that happen?

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:52.825
It is a function of the
insatiable lust for impeachment

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:55.794
in the House
for the past four years.

00:09:55.794 --> 00:09:58.964
-Okay, first of all when you use
the words insatiable lust

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:01.467
in the same room as
Chuck Grassley and Chuck Schumer

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:03.235
it makes me want to
chuck my lunch.

00:10:03.235 --> 00:10:04.503
Just gross, don't do it.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.605
Second, if Democrats
truly had an insatiable lust

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:08.207
for impeachment,
they could've impeached Trump

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:09.375
30 times already.

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:11.344
No President in history
has given Congress

00:10:11.344 --> 00:10:13.412
more cause to impeach
than this guy.

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:15.347
I'd list every impeachable
offense he's committed,

00:10:15.347 --> 00:10:16.648
but I don't have time.

00:10:16.648 --> 00:10:19.118
So instead, for a full recap
of every Trump crime,

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:21.686
just flip on over to our other
channel "Late Night-2."

00:10:21.686 --> 00:10:23.222
It's like ESPN-2,
we have re-runs

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:25.491
of college curling,
minor league polo,

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:28.493
and every sketch where a writer
interrupts me from the audience

00:10:28.493 --> 00:10:30.129
to talk about themselves.

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.832
Now, in a way it's not shocking
Trump has bad lawyers,

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:35.735
because he doesn't need lawyers.

00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:38.704
he's been assured that the GOP
will, with only a few exceptions

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:40.672
pledge total and complete
loyalty to him

00:10:40.672 --> 00:10:43.008
no matter how indefensible his
actions were.

00:10:43.008 --> 00:10:45.644
And that cognitive dissonance
was no full display yesterday

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:48.380
when GOP Senators voted to
dismiss the case,

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.683
and Fox News personalities
tried to discredit the trial

00:10:51.683 --> 00:10:54.253
even as they all complained
about just how bad

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:55.821
the President's lawyers were.

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:59.258
-I thought it started a little
meandering.

00:10:59.258 --> 00:11:00.426
It was sort of like

00:11:00.426 --> 00:11:02.628
a lot of free associating
in the beginning.

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:04.997
-I've seen a lot of lawyers and
a lot of arguments

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:09.635
and that was -- that was not one
of the finest I've seen.

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:10.869
-I thought I knew
where it was going,

00:11:10.869 --> 00:11:12.972
and I really didn't know
where he was going.

00:11:12.972 --> 00:11:15.574
-I would be screaming
if that defense attorney

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:17.075
was defending me.

00:11:17.075 --> 00:11:20.145
He forgot to, I don't know, I
put it here somewhere, prepare.

00:11:20.145 --> 00:11:22.581
-Brian, to your point about
Mr. Castor.

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:26.585
At one point, he compared
manslaughter to murder

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:28.721
which both involve culpability.
-Thanks.

00:11:28.721 --> 00:11:30.723
Which, given the fact that
they're trying to figure out

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:33.025
whether or not
the President incited it,

00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:34.426
it was a bad way to go.

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:36.595
-Wow, you know it's bad whenever
Hannity, Kilmeade, and Ducey

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:37.996
are saying you're unprepared.

00:11:37.996 --> 00:11:40.099
I mean, I'm pretty sure Kilmeade
wears a sign around his neck

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:42.401
that says "If lost return to Fox
and friends."

00:11:42.401 --> 00:11:44.402
Side note, Trump's lawyers are
so
lost they couldn't

00:11:44.402 --> 00:11:47.939
connect the dots between
Brian Kilmeade's extremely

00:11:47.939 --> 00:11:49.408
close together eyes.

00:11:49.408 --> 00:11:51.210
But more importantly,
my question to the Senators

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.645
is this, if Trump's lawyers did
such a bad job,

00:11:53.645 --> 00:11:55.380
then why did you vote with him
anyway?

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.783
Lindsey Graham sounds like he's
describing a movie

00:11:57.783 --> 00:11:59.918
he didn't understand,
but liked anyway.

00:11:59.918 --> 00:12:01.754
[ As Graham ] What I liked about
"Fight Club" is that,

00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:04.023
at it's core,
it's about a friendship

00:12:04.023 --> 00:12:07.426
between Brad Pitt and Ed Norton,
who play two different people.

00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:10.295
But I have to say that one of
the most galling things

00:12:10.295 --> 00:12:11.763
I heard about the trial
yesterday,

00:12:11.763 --> 00:12:14.332
was that as House managers laid
out damning evidence

00:12:14.332 --> 00:12:16.502
of Trump's guilt,
including harrowing scenes

00:12:16.502 --> 00:12:19.104
of violence at the Capitol,
stoked explicitly by the former

00:12:19.104 --> 00:12:21.373
President himself,
several Republican Senators

00:12:21.373 --> 00:12:23.441
couldn't even be bothered
to pay attention.

00:12:23.441 --> 00:12:26.044
-While the Democrats were
playing their video of rioters

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:28.113
storming the Capitol,
a handful of Republican Senators

00:12:28.113 --> 00:12:31.183
including Rick Scott,
Tom Cotton, Marco Rubio,

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:34.819
barely even looked at the screen
according to reports.

00:12:34.819 --> 00:12:37.590
And Rand Paul was looking down
at a paper in his lap

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.625
where he had begun
doodling with a pencil.

00:12:39.625 --> 00:12:41.093
-Of course Rand Paul was
doodling.

00:12:41.093 --> 00:12:42.628
he looks like a doodle
that was

00:12:42.628 --> 00:12:44.062
hit by lightning
and came to life.

00:12:44.062 --> 00:12:45.897
He was probably drawing
a prototype for a new

00:12:45.897 --> 00:12:48.400
ultra weak shower head
to give him even weirder hair.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.136
But hey, if you were a juror,
who had already made up

00:12:51.136 --> 00:12:54.006
your mind how you were gonna
vote, you would doodle too.

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:55.941
They should all come to the
trial with sewing needles

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:57.810
and knit turtlenecks that go all
the way up to

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.245
the top of their heads.

00:12:59.245 --> 00:13:02.314
The President stoked a violent
insurrection at the Capitol

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:04.549
and when presented with damning
video evidence of that fact,

00:13:04.549 --> 00:13:06.118
Republicans
looked the other way,

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:08.287
not just metaphorically,
but literally.

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:09.654
They do not care
that it happened,

00:13:09.654 --> 00:13:11.089
and we have to assume
they wouldn't care

00:13:11.089 --> 00:13:13.225
if it happened again, they're
not even paying attention.

00:13:13.225 --> 00:13:15.160
If you ask them to recap the
arguments,

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:18.363
they'd say there were --
-Comments about --

00:13:18.363 --> 00:13:19.798
I forget what it was.

00:13:19.798 --> 00:13:21.466
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

